ing-only and unhealthy, so it was not a candidate).\n- **Rollback:** The first rollback to v2.3.0 partially failed \u2014 the orchestrator halted after us-east, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I retried, and the second attempt rolled out v2.3.0 to all three regions. Verified afterward: `healthy: true`, error rate 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** Opened **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api) describing the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry), the current healthy state, and follow-ups. The create request timed out, but I confirmed via `list_incidents` that it was created once, so the on-call engineer was paged only once.\n\n**Follow-ups for the on-call engineer** (noted in the incident): root-cause the v2.3.1 failure before any redeploy, and investigate the orchestrator error that interrupted the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}